<title>SINGAPORE: Pengkalen in US$5.0 mln China JV deal.</title>
<headline>Pengkalen in US$5.0 mln China JV deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pengkalen Investments Ltd, the Singapore unit of Malaysian diversified food group Pengkalen Holdings Bhd, said on Monday had struck a US$5.0 million joint venture in the People's Republic of China.</p>
<p>Pengkalen said in a statement its partner in the chocolate, wafer and biscuit manufacturing and retail operation was Qingdao Foods Ltd.</p>
<p>The deal, subject to regulatory approval, would give Pengkalen a 60 percent stake in the joint venture firm Qingdao Network Foods Co Ltd, with Qingdao taking the balance of the shares.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
